  "limits": [
    "Four class bodies and four handles own 244 initialized bytes; final layout and boot integration are unproven. Symbolic handle relocations are verified, not the entire cached-class arena.",
    "Actual cached reader/writer, health wrappers, settings setter and pinned musl memcpy execute; port critical callbacks are modeled. No flash persistence, physical sensor or recovery service proof.",
    "C setter has a 54-byte body plus ten-byte native-frame bridge versus 42 native instruction bytes. No byte identity, complete private-frame/fault/timing identity or provider qualification.",
    "Only the settings setter is converted in native_record_providers.c; existing r1_record12_apply bytes/relocations remain unchanged and its broader behavior remains a separate gate.",
    "Both app and bootloader compile and compose relocatables, not complete firmware. No G2 gate or source-plan change."
  ]
